            {
              "section": "Wolverine Stack Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "Theoretical and stack-level concerns",
              "excerpt": "Both compounds promote angiogenesis, which is the intended mechanism for repair but is also a relevant pathway in tumor growth. A 2003 J Natl Cancer Inst paper by Cha et al. reported that Thymosin Beta-4 expression increased lung-tumor metastasis in a B16-F10 mouse model. The translational meaning for an exogenous TB-500 fragment in humans is unknown, but it is the most-cited theoretical risk in clinician",
              "truncated": true
            },
            {
              "section": "Wolverine Stack Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "Sport and competition",
              "excerpt": "Both BPC-157 and TB-500 are prohibited under WADA's S0 Unapproved Substances category, in and out of competition. Athletes subject to WADA, USADA, or any sport-governing-body testing program should not assume a clearance window — the substances are detectable and prohibited regardless of timing.",
              "truncated": false
            }
          ],
          "independent_verification": false
        },
